html: fit images against the fixed page height (issue #6007)

layout_flow advances ld->bounds through the document. Using those bounds to
calculate the page height makes it zero or negative after the first page, so
the max-height check no longer shrinks later images and they are clipped over
several pages. ld->page retains the fixed pagination rectangle used by the
rest of the layout code.

Fixes https://github.com/sumatrapdfreader/sumatrapdf/issues/6007
---
diff --git a/source/html/html-layout.c b/source/html/html-layout.c
index 7a76cf9f2..e3fc9bf98 100644
--- a/source/html/html-layout.c
+++ b/source/html/html-layout.c
@@ -942,7 +942,7 @@ static void layout_flow(fz_context *ctx, fz_html_box *box, fz_html_box *top, flo
 			float max_w, max_h;
 			float xs = 1, ys = 1, s;
 			float aspect = 1;
-			float page_h = ld->bounds[B] - ld->bounds[T];
+			float page_h = ld->page[B] - ld->page[T];
 
 			max_w = ld->bounds[R] - ld->bounds[L];
 			max_h = page_h;
